prevention. Viruses. (2023) 15:561. doi: 10.3390/v15020561, PMID: [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 19. Song G. Major achievements in prevention and control of epidemic hemorrhagic fever in new China. Chin J Epidemiol. (2000) 21:378–82. doi: 10.3760/j.issn:0254-6450.2000.05.019 [ DOI ] [ Google Scholar ] 20. Zhao R, Dong C, Zhou W, Gu ZF, Gao JL. Research progress on the relationship between human immune senescence and tumor and infection. Natl Med J China. (2019) 99:1278–80. doi: 10.3760/cma.j.issn.0376-2491.2019.16.018 [ DOI ] [ Google Scholar ] 21. Li LJ. Status and control strategy for infectious diseases in China. Chin J Clin Infect Dis. (2008) 1:1–6. doi: 10.3760/cma.j.issn.1674-2397.2008.01.003 [ DOI ] [ Google Scholar ] 22. World Health Organization . Ten threats to Global Health in 2019. Available at: https://www.who.int/newsroom/spotlight/ten-threats-to-global-health-in-2019 . 23. Xu J, Lei L, Xiao HL. An analysis of the characteristics of disease treatment and admission in infection department of a grassroots comprehensive hospital in recent three years in Chongqing City. Mod Hosp Manag. (2017) 15:43–5. [ Google Scholar ] 24. Zou YS. The current situation of infectious diseases and the construction of prevention and control system in China. J Med Res. (2007) 36:14–17, 29. doi: 10.3969/j.issn.1673-548X.2007.01.005 [ DOI ] [ Google Scholar ] 25. Harris E. Measles outbreaks grow amid declining vaccination rates. JAMA. (2023) 330:2242. doi: 10.1001/jama.2023.23511, PMID: [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 26. Yao YH, Xu GJ. The promulgation and implementation of the law on prevention and control of infectious diseases and the development trend of preventive medicine. Mod Prev Med. (2005) 32:756–7. doi: 10.3969/j.issn.1003-8507.2005.07.025 [ DOI ] [ Google Scholar ] Associated Data This section collects any data citations, data availability statements, or supplementary materials included in this article. Data Availability Statement 