Network (IDPN). In: Kuo SHS, Shih WY, Lin T, et al., eds. Taiwan CDC Annual Report 2005. Taipei: Center for Disease Control, Department of Health, R.O.C. (Taiwan); October 2005:31-33 [ Google Scholar ] 13. Establishment of Communicable Disease Control Medical Network. In: Chang FY, Wu YC, Li TF, et al., eds. A Decade After SARS—Lessons Learned and Preparedness. Taipei: Center for Disease Control, Ministry of Health and Welfare, R.O.C. (Taiwan); July 2013:36-39 [ Google Scholar ] 14. Center for Disease Control, Ministry of Health and Welfare R.O.C. (Taiwan). Promotion plan of strategy adjustment on responding hospitals of Communicable Disease Control Medical Network. 2015. http://www.cdc.gov.tw/professional/info.aspx?treeid=10E4730DBC2EB10F&nowtreeid=86A50684EE54F4B8&tid=644AB0348E10CB34 Accessed November16, 2016 15. Center for Disease Control, Ministry of Health and Welfare R.O.C. (Taiwan). Principal of the activation of responding hospitals and operation of support workforce in Communicable Disease Control Medical Network. 2015. http://www.cdc.gov.tw/professional/info.aspx?treeid=10e4730dbc2eb10f&nowtreeid=eed17251205b4e37&tid=DA26436E9AE7F61A Accessed November16, 2016 16. Center for Disease Control, Department of Health R.O.C. (Taiwan). Taiwan''s response to the H1N1 influenza pandemic. Taipei: Center for Disease Control, Department of Health, R.O.C. (Taiwan); August 2011 [ Google Scholar ] 17. Guo P, Lin MH, Lin M, Chou SM, Chen CH. Response measures of the Communicable Disease Control Medical Network to H1N1 novel influenza. Epidemiol Bull 2010;26:409-415 [ Google Scholar ] 18. 2009 focus H1N1 pandemic preparedness and response. In: Chang FY, Shih WY, Lin T, et al., eds. Taiwan CDC Annual Report 2010. Taipei: Center for Disease Control, Department of Health, R.O.C. (Taiwan); July 2010:10-19 [ Google Scholar ] 19. World Health Organization. Statement on the 1 st meeting of the IHR Emergency Committee on the 2014 Ebola outbreak in West Africa. August 8, 2014. http://www.who.int/ mediacentre/news/statements/2014/ebola-20140808/en/ Accessed November16, 2016 20. Kao HY, Lin MH, Chih YC, Chou SM, Yang CH. The current Ebola outbreak in West Africa and the response measures in Taiwan. Epidemiol Bull 2014;30:335-339 [ Google Scholar ] 21. Emerging infectious diseases (EID) response. In: Kuo SHS, Chou JH, Chuang JH, et al., eds. Taiwan CDC Annual Report 2015. Taipei: Center for Disease Control, Ministry of Health and Welfare, R.O.C. (Taiwan); August 2015:50-53 [ Google Scholar ] 22. Hsu SM, Chien LJ, Tseng SH, Kuo SHS. A no-notice drill of hospital preparedness in responding to Ebola virus disease in Taiwan. Health Secur 2015;13(5):339-344 [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 23. van Beneden CA, Pietz H, Kirkcaldy RD, et al. Early identification and prevention of the spread of Ebola—United States. MMWR Suppl 2016;65(Suppl 3):75-84 [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 24. Cummings KJ, Choi MJ, Esswein EJ, et al. Addressing infection prevention and control in the first U.S. community hospital to care for patients with Ebola virus disease: context for national recommendations and future strategies. Ann Intern Med 2016;165:41-49 [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 25. National Ebola Treatment and Education Center website. http://netec.org/ Accessed November16, 2016',7,'2025-10-10 06:39:54','2025-10-10 06:39:54');
INSERT INTO corpus VALUES(1032,'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7132650','Emerging infectious diseases: Focus on infection control issues for novel coronaviruses (Severe Acute Respiratory Syndrome-CoV and Middle East Respiratory Syndrome-CoV), hemorrhagic fever viruses (Lassa and Ebola), and highly pathogenic avian influenza viruses, A(H5N1) and A(H7N9).','Weber DJ, Rutala WA, Fischer WA, Kanamori H, Sickbert-Bennett EE.','2016','pestilence laureate legionnaires legionella legionella legionella breakdowns protozoa climactic technologic jumped karesh encroachment deforestation reforestation drought famine curtailment exotic exotic arthropods legionella legionella legionnaires nap1 germicide communicability germicide postexposure solids arenaviridae filoviridae coronaviridae coronaviridae orthomyxoviridae enveloped enveloped enveloped enveloped enveloped camels civet nonintact nonintact biothreat neuraminidase postexposure nestle signage purifier preventionist spill nonintact dispose wastes disinfectant nonenveloped enveloped disinfectant enveloped nonenveloped nonenveloped nonenveloped spores arenaviridae serologically mobala junin machupo sabia choriomeningitis multimammate mastomys natalensis mastomys droppings soiled nonintact excretions missionary adenopathy germicide enveloped phenolics suitably postexposure nonsegmented filoviridae zaire bundibugyo reston insectivore nonintact vomit recrudescent bushmeat zaire myalgias arthralgias maculopapular zaire bundibugyo reston transgenically nicotiana benthamiana fomite sterilized sterilized coronaviridae himalayan civets raccoon horseshoe rhinolophus sinicus superspreaders trading superspreading myalgias hanoi glutaraldehyde phenolics hcov229e sizun sponges latex postinoculation glutaraldehyde phenolics camels dromedary humped camels mutates tawfiq intrahospital notifying superspreaders recoverable washers fomite phenolics enveloped orthomyxoviridae neuraminidase virions neuraminidase h17 n10 h2n20 h3n2 reintr